  "summary": "A distinctive printmaking tradition developed by Inuit artists in Kinngait, characterized by bold lines and stylized depictions of Arctic wildlife and traditional life.",
  "description": "The aesthetic features simplified forms with strong outlines and limited color palettes, developed from traditional graphic arts adapted to printmaking techniques. It emerged from the West Baffin Eskimo Co-operative established in 1959, transforming Inuit visual narratives into widely accessible artworks.",
